Docker–Nginx Deployment (Short)
1.	Created an Azure VM (Ubuntu) and installed Docker
2.	Created a Dockerfile with Nginx and custom index.html
3.	Built a Docker image using:
4.	docker build -t custom-nginx .
5.	Tagged and pushed the image to Docker Hub
6.	Pulled the image from Docker Hub and ran the container on port 80
7.	Created Azure Container Registry (ACR)
8.	Logged in to ACR using admin credentials
9.	Tagged the same image and pushed it to ACR
10.	Verified the image in ACR repositories
11.	Accessed the Nginx app using the VM Public IP
